WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.640
Turn a newt's eye upside down, then cut the optic nerve and let it regrow.

2
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.220
Hold a lure above its head, and the newt turns its head down.

3
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.720
It kept making that mistake for as long as anyone watched.

4
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.200
Sperry inferred that each regrown axon went back to the place it came from.

5
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.200
How does an axon know where to go?

6
00:00:21.883 --> 00:00:26.203
The retina sends its axons to a target in the midbrain, the tectum.

7
00:00:26.563 --> 00:00:27.643
The map is orderly.

8
00:00:28.203 --> 00:00:31.023
Neighbors in the retina connect to neighbors in the tectum.

9
00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:36.483
In the chick, axons from the temporal retina, the side nearer the temple, end in the

10
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:37.563
front of the tectum.

11
00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:40.023
Nasal axons end in the back.

12
00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.107
A growth cone is the moving tip of an axon.

13
00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:47.427
It senses only what is close, yet the map spans the whole target.

14
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:50.207
The answer is a pair of opposite slopes.

15
00:00:51.087 --> 00:00:56.447
In the retina, the receptor FA is high on the temporal side and low on the nasal

16
00:00:56.447 --> 00:01:01.347
side. In the tectum, the ligand Efron A rises from front to back.

17
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:08.200
Temporal axons carry the most FA, so a little Efrin A repels them.

18
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.860
Their endings form in the front of the tectum.

19
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.700
Nasal axons carry little FA and tolerate more ephrin, so their endings form farther

20
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:22.200
back. In chicken mouse, axons first overshoot, then branch, and Efrin a blocks

21
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.640
branches behind the right zone.

22
00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:29.633
An axon might read an absolute level of FA or compare itself with its neighbours.

23
00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:35.593
In mouse, researchers gave a scattered half of the retinal ganglion cells extra FA.

24
00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:40.833
If axons read absolute levels, only those cells should shift forward.

25
00:01:41.293 --> 00:01:46.333
Instead, with two copies of the knock -in, the cells with extra FA took the front of

26
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:49.553
the target, and their normal neighbours were pushed to the back.

27
00:01:50.153 --> 00:01:52.513
Two orderly maps filled the target together.

28
00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:55.827
So each axon is judged against the others.

29
00:01:56.427 --> 00:01:59.607
Its ending depends on its EFA signal relative to its neighbours.

30
00:02:00.527 --> 00:02:03.387
Axons compete for space, and the map is the outcome.

31
00:02:04.007 --> 00:02:06.507
Each growth cone senses only a short distance.

32
00:02:06.947 --> 00:02:11.627
Yet local rules give global order, partly because axons also sense each other.
